IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Texas Human Resources Code Chapter 31 -- Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF cash assistance, "financial
-- assistance" in the chapter), from the seat of the applicant or recipient: the parent or relative applying for a
-- dependent child.
--
-- In scope: who is a "dependent child" (s 31.002(a)); proof of citizenship or immigration status and residence, and of
-- immunization within 180 days (s 31.031(c)-(e)); identifying the other parent (s 31.0315); the resources left out
-- (s 31.032(d), s 31.0039) and the income left out (ss 31.0036, 31.0038); the time limits and when they start
-- (s 31.0065); the work requirement and its exemptions (s 31.012(a), (c)); the responsibility agreement (s 31.0031(d)),
-- the sanction for not cooperating and how long it lasts (s 31.0032(a), (a-1)), the 13 days to ask for a good cause hearing
-- (s 31.0033(a)), two months of non-cooperation (s 31.00331); moving out of state (s 31.036); reporting more income
-- (s 31.033(e)); the one-time supplemental payment for a grandparent or other relative (s 31.0041).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the amount of assistance (s 31.003 leaves it to rules; the grant table is HHSC's Texas Works Handbook
-- Appendix C-110, indexed but not deposited: see the state README) and the resource limit itself (rules); the foster-care
-- branch of "dependent child" (s 31.002(b)); programme and interagency duties (ss 31.006 to 31.0129, 31.015 to 31.018);
-- payment machinery (ss 31.035 to 31.045 except s 31.036); the state budget limits (ss 31.051 to 31.053).
--
-- Edition: Tex. Hum. Res. Code ch. 31 as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/tex-hum-res-code-ch31.txt (Texas
-- Legislative Council chapter file dated 2026-09-01, retrieved 2026-10-19).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Texas TANF (Human Resources Code chapter 31) -- the applicant's and recipient's questions`

§§ `s 31.002(a) -- is my child a "dependent child"`

-- s 31.002(a): a child "(1) who is a resident of this state; (2) who is under 18 years of age or is under 19 years of age
-- and is a full-time student in a secondary school or at the equivalent level of vocational or technical training if,
-- before the child's 19th birthday, the child may reasonably be expected to complete the secondary school or training
-- program; (3) who has been deprived of parental support or care because of the death, continued absence from home, or
-- physical or mental incapacity of a parent; (4) who has insufficient income or other resources to provide a reasonable
-- subsistence compatible with health and decency; and (5) who is living in the home residence of his or her father,
-- mother, grandfather, grandmother, brother, sister, stepfather, stepmother, stepbrother, stepsister, uncle, aunt, first
-- cousin, nephew, or niece." Item (4) is the commission's standard of need, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Who the child lives with` IS ONE OF
    `a relative listed in s 31.002(a)(5)`
    `someone else`
    `in foster care through the Department of Family and Protective Services`

DECLARE `Why deprived` IS ONE OF
    `a parent has died`
    `a parent is continually absent from home`
    `a parent is physically or mentally incapacitated`
    `not deprived of a parent's support or care`

DECLARE `Dependent child answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, a dependent child (s 31.002(a))`
    `no, not a dependent child under s 31.002(a)`
    `not covered: a child in foster care is under s 31.002(b), which is not encoded`

GIVEN `lives in Texas` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age` IS A NUMBER
      `full-time secondary or vocational student expected to finish before 19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deprivation` IS A `Why deprived`
      `insufficient income and resources` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lives with` IS A `Who the child lives with`
GIVETH A `Dependent child answer`
`dependent child` MEANS
    IF `lives with` EQUALS `in foster care through the Department of Family and Protective Services`
    THEN `not covered: a child in foster care is under s 31.002(b), which is not encoded`
    ELSE IF     `lives in Texas`
            AND (`age` LESS THAN 18 OR (`age` LESS THAN 19 AND `full-time secondary or vocational student expected to finish before 19`))
            AND (NOT (`deprivation` EQUALS `not deprived of a parent's support or care`))
            AND `insufficient income and resources`
            AND `lives with` EQUALS `a relative listed in s 31.002(a)(5)`
         THEN `yes, a dependent child (s 31.002(a))`
         ELSE `no, not a dependent child under s 31.002(a)`

@export Is my child a "dependent child" for Texas TANF (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.002(a))?
GIVEN `my child lives in Texas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a resident of Texas
      `my child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in years
      `my child is a full-time student expected to finish before turning 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the child is 18, whether the child is a full-time student in secondary school (or the equivalent vocational or technical training) and can reasonably be expected to finish before turning 19
      `why the child lacks a parent's support or care` IS A `Why deprived` @desc Why the child is deprived of a parent's support or care: "a parent has died", "a parent is continually absent from home", "a parent is physically or mentally incapacitated", or "not deprived of a parent's support or care"
      `the child's own income and resources are not enough to live on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child has insufficient income or other resources to provide a reasonable subsistence compatible with health and decency (the commission's standard of need)
      `who the child lives with` IS A `Who the child lives with` @desc Whose home the child lives in: "a relative listed in s 31.002(a)(5)" (father, mother, grandparent, brother, sister, step-parent, step-sibling, uncle, aunt, first cousin, nephew or niece), "someone else", or "in foster care through the Department of Family and Protective Services"
GIVETH A `Dependent child answer`
`Is my child a dependent child` MEANS
    `dependent child` `my child lives in Texas` `my child's age` `my child is a full-time student expected to finish before turning 19` `why the child lacks a parent's support or care` `the child's own income and resources are not enough to live on` `who the child lives with`

§§ `ss 31.032(d), 31.0039 -- resources left out`

-- s 31.032(d): "the commission shall exclude from the applicant's available resources: (1) $1,000 for the applicant's
-- household, including a household in which there is a person with a disability or a person who is at least 60 years of
-- age; and (2) the fair market value of the applicant's ownership interest in a motor vehicle, but not more than $5,000
-- plus or minus an amount to be determined annually beginning on October 1, 1997, to reflect changes in the new car
-- component of the Consumer Price Index". The indexed vehicle figure is an input. s 31.0039: Texas prepaid tuition and
-- college savings plans (Education Code ch. 54, subchs. G, H, I) and similar plans are not considered.
-- "A motor vehicle" (singular): one vehicle's value is excluded, the most valuable taken (NOTES.md finding 4).
@export How much of my household's resources count for Texas TANF after the exclusions in Tex. Hum. Res. Code ss 31.032(d) and 31.0039?
GIVEN `our resources other than vehicles and college savings` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value in US dollars of the household's resources other than motor vehicles and college savings or prepaid tuition plans (cash, bank accounts, other property the commission counts)
      `my vehicle with the highest value` IS A NUMBER @desc The fair market value of your ownership interest in your most valuable motor vehicle (0 if none)
      `my other vehicles` IS A NUMBER @desc The total fair market value of your ownership interest in any other motor vehicles
      `the vehicle exclusion this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle exclusion currently in force: $5,000 adjusted each October 1 since 1997 by the new car component of the CPI-U
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our resources count` MEANS
        (max 0 (`our resources other than vehicles and college savings` MINUS 1000))
    PLUS (max 0 (`my vehicle with the highest value` MINUS `the vehicle exclusion this year`))
    PLUS `my other vehicles`

§§ `ss 31.0036, 31.0038 -- income left out`

-- s 31.0036: "may not consider any income earned by a dependent child who is attending school and whose income is derived
-- from the child's part-time employment". s 31.0038: "income earned by an individual who marries an individual receiving
-- financial assistance at the time of the marriage may not be considered ... during the six-month period following the
-- date of the marriage", if "the combined income of the individual receiving financial assistance and the new spouse
-- cannot exceed 200 percent of the federal poverty level for their family size" (the poverty level is an input).
@export Is my new spouse's income left out for Texas TANF (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0038)?
GIVEN `I was receiving TANF when we married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were receiving Texas TANF at the time of the marriage
      `the day we married` IS A DATE @desc The date of the marriage
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day (or the month's first day) you are asking about
      `our combined income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your and your new spouse's combined income for the period, in US dollars
      `200 percent of the poverty level for our family size` IS A NUMBER @desc 200% of the federal poverty level for your family size for the same period, in US dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my new spouse's income left out` IF
        `I was receiving TANF when we married`
    AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day we married`
    AND `the day asked about` LESS THAN (`add months` `the day we married` 6)
    AND `our combined income` AT MOST `200 percent of the poverty level for our family size`

@export How much of my household's earned income counts for Texas TANF once a schoolchild's part-time earnings are left out (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0036)?
GIVEN `the household's earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc All earnings of the household for the period, in US dollars, including any child's
      `part-time earnings of dependent children attending school` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of those earnings that dependent children who attend school earn from part-time jobs
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our earned income counts` MEANS
    max 0 (`the household's earned income` MINUS `part-time earnings of dependent children attending school`)

§§ `s 31.0065 -- how long I can get TANF`

-- s 31.0065(b): the cumulative limit of financial assistance, by the person receiving it on behalf of the child:
-- "(1) ... 12 months ... if the person ... has: (A) a high school diploma, a high school equivalency certificate, or a
-- certificate or degree from a two-year or four-year institution of higher education or technical or vocational school; or
-- (B) recent work experience of 18 months or more; (2) ... 24 months ... if the person ... has: (A) completed three years of
-- high school; or (B) recent work experience of not less than six or more than 18 months; and (3) ... 36 months ... if the
-- person ... has: (A) completed less than three years of high school; and (B) less than six months of work experience."
-- Transitional benefits are 12 months in each case. The tiers are tried in order, so 18 months of work falls in (1)
-- (NOTES.md finding 2). (f)(1): where the needs assessment shows a lower functional level, it governs (an input).
-- (a): the executive commissioner may provide hardship exceptions by rule (an input).
DECLARE `Education` IS ONE OF
    `high school diploma, equivalency certificate, or a college, technical or vocational certificate or degree`
    `completed three years of high school`
    `completed less than three years of high school`

GIVEN `education` IS AN `Education`
      `months of recent work experience` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the time limit in months` MEANS
    IF     `education` EQUALS `high school diploma, equivalency certificate, or a college, technical or vocational certificate or degree`
        OR `months of recent work experience` AT LEAST 18
    THEN 12
    ELSE IF     `education` EQUALS `completed three years of high school`
             OR `months of recent work experience` AT LEAST 6
         THEN 24
         ELSE 36

@export How many months of Texas TANF can I receive under the state time limits (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0065(b))?
GIVEN `my education` IS AN `Education` @desc Your education (the functional level found in your needs assessment, if lower): "high school diploma, equivalency certificate, or a college, technical or vocational certificate or degree", "completed three years of high school", or "completed less than three years of high school"
      `my recent work experience in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of recent work experience you have
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many months of TANF can I receive` MEANS
    `the time limit in months` `my education` `my recent work experience in months`

-- s 31.0065(d): "The computation of time limits ... begins when the adult or teen parent recipient receives notification
-- ... of the availability of an opening in and eligibility for a Temporary Assistance for Needy Families employment
-- program". (c): for the 36-month tier, if the recipient cooperates with the in-depth assessment, "the time period
-- prescribed by Subsection (b)(3) begins on the first anniversary of the date on which the commission completes the
-- assessment". (e)(1): "a participant ... may reapply ... on or after the fifth anniversary of the date on which the
-- participant is totally disqualified".
@export From what date does my Texas TANF time limit start to run (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0065(c), (d))?
GIVEN `the day I was notified of an opening in the TANF employment program` IS A DATE @desc The day you received notice that there is an opening for you in the TANF employment program and that you are eligible for it
      `I am in the 36-month tier and cooperated with the in-depth assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have less than three years of high school and less than six months of work experience, and cooperated with the commission's in-depth assessment of your needs
      `the day the commission completed the assessment` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the commission completed that assessment
GIVETH A DATE
`When does my time limit start` MEANS
    IF `I am in the 36-month tier and cooperated with the in-depth assessment`
    THEN `add years` `the day the commission completed the assessment` 1
    ELSE `the day I was notified of an opening in the TANF employment program`

@export If I used up my Texas TANF months, from what date may I reapply (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0065(e)(1))?
GIVEN `the day I was totally disqualified by the time limit` IS A DATE @desc The day you became totally disqualified from assistance because you reached your time limit
GIVETH A DATE
`When may I reapply after the time limit` MEANS `add years` `the day I was totally disqualified by the time limit` 5

§§ `s 31.012 -- must I work or take part in the employment program`

-- s 31.012(a): during any month an adult receives financial assistance, the adult shall "(1) work not less than 30 hours a
-- week; or (2) participate for not less than 20 hours a week in an activity established under a Temporary Assistance for
-- Needy Families employment program". (c): not required: "the caretaker of a child with a physical disability or mental,
-- intellectual, or developmental disability who requires the caretaker's presence"; "A single person who is the caretaker
-- of a child is exempt until the caretaker's youngest child at the time the caretaker first became eligible for assistance
-- reaches the age of one."
DECLARE `Work answer` IS ONE OF
    `exempt: I care for a child with a disability who needs me there (s 31.012(c))`
    `exempt until my youngest child (when I first became eligible) turns one (s 31.012(c))`
    `I meet the work requirement this month (s 31.012(a))`
    `I do not meet the work requirement this month: I must work 30 hours a week or take part 20 hours a week in the employment program (s 31.012(a))`

@export Do I meet the Texas TANF work requirement this month (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.012)?
GIVEN `I care for a child with a disability who needs me there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the caretaker of a child with a physical, mental, intellectual or developmental disability who requires your presence
      `I am a single caretaker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a single person who is the caretaker of a child (the parent or relative the child mainly lives with)
      `my youngest child when I first became eligible is under one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the youngest child you had when you first became eligible for assistance is still under one year old
      `hours I work each week` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours a week you work
      `hours I take part in the TANF employment program each week` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours a week you take part in an activity of the TANF employment program
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`Do I meet the work requirement` MEANS
    IF `I care for a child with a disability who needs me there`
    THEN `exempt: I care for a child with a disability who needs me there (s 31.012(c))`
    ELSE IF `I am a single caretaker` AND `my youngest child when I first became eligible is under one`
         THEN `exempt until my youngest child (when I first became eligible) turns one (s 31.012(c))`
         ELSE IF `hours I work each week` AT LEAST 30 OR `hours I take part in the TANF employment program each week` AT LEAST 20
              THEN `I meet the work requirement this month (s 31.012(a))`
              ELSE `I do not meet the work requirement this month: I must work 30 hours a week or take part 20 hours a week in the employment program (s 31.012(a))`

§§ `ss 31.0031, 31.0032, 31.0033, 31.00331 -- the responsibility agreement and sanctions`

-- s 31.0031(d): the agreement requires (1) cooperation on paternity and child support; (2) children's health checkups and
-- immunizations (where providers are available); (3) not voluntarily quitting paid work of at least 30 hours a week without
-- good cause; (4) an activity toward self-sufficiency where a needs assessment is done; (5) no illegal drug use, sale or
-- possession, and no alcohol abuse; (6) school attendance by each dependent child under 18 or teen parent under 19 without
-- a diploma or exemption; (7) proof of school attendance; (8) parenting skills classes as the needs assessment decides.
-- s 31.0032(a): on a finding of non-cooperation "the commission shall immediately apply a sanction terminating the total
-- amount of financial assistance ... to or for the person and the person's family". (a-1): "for a period ending when the
-- person demonstrates cooperation ... or for a one-month period, whichever is longer".
-- s 31.00331: "A person who fails to cooperate with the responsibility agreement for two consecutive months becomes
-- ineligible", and on reapplying "must cooperate ... for a one-month period before receiving an assistance payment".
DECLARE `Sanction answer` IS ONE OF
    `no sanction: I am cooperating with the responsibility agreement`
    `no sanction yet: my good cause hearing request was in time, so payment may not be withheld until good cause is decided (s 31.0033(a))`
    `the whole family's assistance stops until I show cooperation, and for at least one month (s 31.0032(a), (a-1))`
    `the family is ineligible after two consecutive months of not cooperating; on reapplying I must cooperate for a month before a payment (s 31.00331)`

@export What happens to my family's Texas TANF if I am found not to be cooperating with my responsibility agreement (Tex. Hum. Res. Code ss 31.0032, 31.0033, 31.00331)?
GIVEN `I have been found not to be cooperating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commission or the child support (Title IV-D) agency has determined that you are not cooperating with a requirement of your responsibility agreement
      `consecutive months of not cooperating` IS A NUMBER @desc How many consecutive months you have not cooperated
      `I asked for a good cause hearing by the 13th day after the notice was sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the person receiving the assistance) asked for a hearing to show good cause not later than the 13th day after the date the commission sent its notice
      `good cause has been decided against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commission has held the hearing and found good cause was not shown
GIVETH A `Sanction answer`
`What happens if I am not cooperating` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I have been found not to be cooperating`)
    THEN `no sanction: I am cooperating with the responsibility agreement`
    ELSE IF `consecutive months of not cooperating` AT LEAST 2
         THEN `the family is ineligible after two consecutive months of not cooperating; on reapplying I must cooperate for a month before a payment (s 31.00331)`
         ELSE IF `I asked for a good cause hearing by the 13th day after the notice was sent` AND (NOT `good cause has been decided against me`)
              THEN `no sanction yet: my good cause hearing request was in time, so payment may not be withheld until good cause is decided (s 31.0033(a))`
              ELSE `the whole family's assistance stops until I show cooperation, and for at least one month (s 31.0032(a), (a-1))`

-- s 31.0033(e): good cause for not cooperating on paternity and child support (s 31.0031(d)(1)) "only if: (1) the person's
-- cooperation would be harmful to the physical, mental, or emotional health of the person or the person's dependent child;
-- or (2) the person's noncooperation resulted from other circumstances the person could not control" (subject to a family
-- violence waiver under s 31.0322).
@export Do I have good cause for not cooperating on paternity and child support (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0033(e))?
GIVEN `cooperating would harm my or my child's physical, mental or emotional health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether cooperating would be harmful to your or your dependent child's physical, mental or emotional health
      `I could not control the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your non-cooperation resulted from other circumstances you could not control
      `I have a family violence waiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commission has granted you a waiver or modification for family violence under s 31.0322
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have good cause on child support` IF
        `cooperating would harm my or my child's physical, mental or emotional health`
    OR  `I could not control the circumstances`
    OR  `I have a family violence waiver`

§§ `Duties and deadlines, in days`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant or recipient`
    `the commission`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `give proof of the child's immunization`
    `notify the commission of more income or resources`
    `request a good cause hearing`

-- s 31.031(d), (e): proof that each child five or younger, or not in public school, is immunized, receiving the series, or
-- exempt; "An applicant who cannot provide the proof ... at the time of application shall provide the proof not later than
-- the 180th day after the date the commission determines the applicant is eligible". Days from that determination.
-- The chapter states no consequence; sanctions are by rule under s 31.0031(c) (finding 6).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to prove immunization` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
    MUST  `give proof of the child's immunization`
    WITHIN 180
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant or recipient` BECAUSE "proof of immunization was not given by the 180th day after eligibility was determined (s 31.031(e))"

-- s 31.033(e): "A recipient of assistance must notify the commission immediately if he or she comes into possession of
-- income or resources in excess of the amount previously reported." "Immediately" is modelled as within one day of
-- receipt (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to report more income` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
    MUST  `notify the commission of more income or resources`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant or recipient` BECAUSE "income or resources above the amount reported were not notified immediately (s 31.033(e))"

-- s 31.0033(a): the person "may request a hearing to show good cause for failure to cooperate not later than the 13th day
-- after the date the notice is sent under Section 31.0032". Days from the day the notice was sent.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my right to a good cause hearing` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
    MAY   `request a good cause hearing`
    WITHIN 13

@export By what date must I give proof of my child's immunization for Texas TANF (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.031(e))?
GIVEN `the day I was found eligible` IS A DATE @desc The day the commission determined you eligible for assistance
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I prove immunization` MEANS `the day I was found eligible` PLUS 180

@export By what date must I ask for a good cause hearing after a non-cooperation notice (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0033(a))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc The date the commission sent the notice that assistance will not be paid because of a failure to cooperate
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask for a good cause hearing` MEANS `the day the notice was sent` PLUS 13

§§ `s 31.036 -- moving out of Texas (only if I leave the State)`

-- s 31.036: "A recipient of assistance who moves out of the state is no longer eligible for the assistance. However, a
-- recipient's temporary absence from the state for reasons and for periods of time approved by the commission does not
-- terminate the recipient's eligibility".
@export If I leave Texas, do I keep my TANF (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.036)?
GIVEN `I have moved out of Texas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have moved your home out of Texas (rather than being away temporarily)
      `I am temporarily away from Texas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are away from Texas for a while without having moved
      `the commission approved my temporary absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are away temporarily, whether the commission approved the reason for and length of your absence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I keep TANF if I leave Texas` IF
        (NOT `I have moved out of Texas`)
    AND (    (NOT `I am temporarily away from Texas`)
         OR  `the commission approved my temporary absence`)

§§ `s 31.0041 -- the one-time payment for a grandparent or other relative raising a child`

-- s 31.0041(a): "To the extent funds are appropriated", the commission "may provide supplemental financial assistance" to a
-- person who "(1) is 25 years of age or older; (2) is the grandparent, aunt, uncle, sister, or brother of the dependent
-- child ... who lives at the person's residence; (3) is the primary caretaker of the dependent child; (4) has a family
-- income that is at or below 200 percent of the federal poverty level; and (5) does not have resources that exceed the
-- amount allowed". (b): "one or more cash payments, not to exceed a total of $1,000". (e): only one person per child.
@export Can I get the Texas supplemental payment of up to $1,000 as a grandparent or other relative raising a child (Tex. Hum. Res. Code s 31.0041)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I am the child's grandparent, aunt, uncle, sister or brother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the dependent child's grandparent, aunt, uncle, sister or brother
      `the child lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives at your home
      `I am the child's primary caretaker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the child's primary caretaker
      `my family income is at or below 200 percent of the poverty level` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family income is at or below 200% of the federal poverty level
      `my resources are within the TANF limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your resources do not exceed the amount allowed for TANF
      `someone else already received it for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person has already received this supplemental payment for the same child
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Most supplemental payment I can get` MEANS
    IF     `my age` AT LEAST 25
       AND `I am the child's grandparent, aunt, uncle, sister or brother`
       AND `the child lives with me`
       AND `I am the child's primary caretaker`
       AND `my family income is at or below 200 percent of the poverty level`
       AND `my resources are within the TANF limit`
       AND (NOT `someone else already received it for this child`)
    THEN 1000
    ELSE 0
